  "_dshV2_comment": "ADDED 2026-08-26. Config for the DSH-V2 long-only ADX-gated breakout (see 'DSH backtesting/' and app/scripts/verify-dsh-strategy.js). shadowOnly:true and liveSize:null are the load-bearing values - this strategy has NEVER traded and nothing here may place an order; the CONTROL toggle's own gate is the second lock. shadowSizes [4,6] records the SAME signals at BOTH sizes simultaneously because Anoop wants to try 6 contracts and the 9-month backtest says 4 dominates it: over 234 rolling one-month windows, 4c cleared the $3,000 target in 16% of months with ZERO blow-ups, while 6c cleared it in 18% with 15% blow-ups. That is +2 points of success for +15 points of ruin, and the $2,000 floor falls precisely between them (worst month -$1,488 at 4c vs -$2,233 at 6c). Shadowing both costs nothing and settles it on his own forward data instead of on my argument or his hunch. NOTE sizeCap is 2: trading EITHER size live requires deliberately raising it, and the last time this account was oversized against a stated cap (2026-07-21, 150K eval) it breached - see _sizeCap_comment. dailyCapPer2Contracts scales with size and enforces the 40% consistency rule.",
  "autonomyEnabled": false,
  "_autonomyEnabled_comment": "SET FALSE 2026-08-26 at Anoop's instruction: \"disable shadow mode and control mode until i start working on them and have a proper plan. i want to focus on trading and reaching payout rather then build further and confuse. i want only you mode from now on.\" This is a HARD kill switch, checked before the toggle is even offered - the CONTROL toggle is hidden in the UI, the autonomy WebSocket handlers refuse, and both shadow recorders and the shadow resolver are inert. Nothing is deleted: DATA/autonomy/ keeps its record and every module stays under test, so turning this back to true restores the whole thing without a rebuild. Also removes real load from the single TradingView connection - the shadow resolver was one more 5-minute chart reader competing with the watchers.",
  "_eval_comment": "start CORRECTED 2026-08-28 from 150000 to 50378.60, flagged by Protocol 1's account-coherence check. Anoop trades 50K accounts; renderer ACCOUNT_PROFILES and DATA/accounts/s1/meta.json were both corrected earlier and this file was missed, so rules.json and the renderer disagreed about the same account. 50378.60 is DERIVED (broker balance minus the ledger's net days), not read from an opening statement - replace it when the real figure is to hand. profitTarget and maxDrawdown below are STILL THE 150K FIGURES and are deliberately left alone: they drive the live drawdown guard, and writing a guessed 3000/2000 into a safety limit is worse than a known-wrong one that is documented. Anoop must confirm the real 50K target and drawdown from the Tradeify dashboard before those two change."
